{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread","id":261707,"title":"Where Wolves Don't Tread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T20:24:54-07:00","id":261707,"title":"Where Wolves Don't Tread","content":"In nature, wolves are all over the place. Go just about anywhere and there'll be wolves (or other wild canines) hanging around. The two major exceptions are oceans (obviously) and jungles. How does this affect your Werewolf games? Do Uratha work in the jungle regardless? Do they hop into boats and sail around fixing Deep Sea Problems? If they don't, does anything take care of spirit problems there or is it just a big HERE BE DRAGONS on their maps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T20:43:57-07:00","id":261731,"title":"","content":"This is a slightly easier issue to handle in WtF than in WtA, since all Uratha are born in human form to human or Uratha parents. There are Uratha in areas where there are no wolves. They just need to be all the more careful for the fact that their Urhan forms are going to stand out as an abnormal presence - but that's not necessarily any more true in a jungle than in a major metropolitan area. At my own table, many South American Uratha have canine features somewhat closer to those of maned wolves, rather than Canis Lupus wolves, though often bulkier than &quot;normal&quot; maned wolves.<br /> <br /> The ocean is a definite issue. There are likely a handful of lodges that make a point of trying to carry out their hunts upon the sea - but the ocean depths are as alien to the Uratha as they are to humanity - and there are likely a multitude of spirit horrors/host/claimed-sea-beasts, etc that are free to breed in the briny deeps.... until they threaten the material or Hisil shore.<br /> <br /> This remains why I think a hardback gameline focused on oceanic horror - with a Deep One inspired pc species - would be a strong addition to the WoD. Leviathan the Tempest is the fan project that comes closest to what I'm imagining, and I recommend it to those looking for the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T20:53:39-07:00","id":261740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=261731#post261731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Canis lupus</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected for format.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T23:27:24-07:00","id":261858,"title":"","content":"I think glamourweaver covered the important stuff pretty succinctly, and pointed out the lack of Oceanic coverage in books.<br /> <br /> In first edition there was the Anybeast gift that let werewolves take the form of different (but not too different) animals. In Central and South America, it was common for werewolves to choose to appear as jaguars, to the point that it's a tradition to have mastery of the gift to one of the areas lodges (the Lodge of Quetzal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T02:48:06-07:00","id":261970,"title":"","content":"At least as the 1e goes, the bigger question is what do Werewolves do about places that humans don't live in? They need humans to reproduce after all.<br /> <br /> From that perspective Antarctica is probably an even bigger problem than the sea or jungles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T04:52:55-07:00","id":262014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=261731#post261731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This remains why I think a hardback gameline focused on oceanic horror - with a Deep One inspired pc species - would be a strong addition to the WoD. Leviathan the Tempest is the fan project that comes closest to what I'm imagining, and I recommend it to those looking for the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see a Book of the Dead style bluebook that ties into Leviathan and focuses on just what's under the sea. Sadly the fan-project to create that didn't get very far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T08:09:35-07:00","id":262165,"title":"","content":"There's a reason oceans aren't given a lot of attention.<br /> <br /> Al the action is literally happening on the land.<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, there's a limit to what can happen on the top of the oceans, underneath the waves is limited in terms of access, and it's a serious challenge to make under the sea stuff compelling for a horror setting without crossing over too far into other genres. It can be a little hard to fit directly into WoD's senses.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it can't happen-there's a lot of good oceanic horror out there. But it must be considered that there's a reason why ocean based stories are vastly overwhelmed by land or even sky based stories.<br /> <br /> Not to cop the enitre &quot;Creature of the Black Lagoon&quot; thing harder on it than it needs, because heaven forbid people can't stop talking about it, but I imagine Beast might help open some of the doors.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I'd love to see the Polynesian Islands as a Werewolf setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T08:42:30-07:00","id":262194,"title":"","content":"I think it's likely that Beast will let you play acquatic creatures. But I think it will end up like Changeling, or even Vampire. You have all the tools you need to play an acquatic charachter, and no advice on why you might go for a swim and what you'd find there.<br /> <br /> You're right that ocean stories are vastly overwhelmed, but that just means there's more need for supporting material to cover that ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T10:05:58-07:00","id":262246,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna keep quietly hoping for an official book on sea stuff. Blood-Dimmed Tides wasn't half bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T11:59:48-07:00","id":262337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=261970#post261970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least as the 1e goes, the bigger question is what do Werewolves do about places that humans don't live in? They need humans to reproduce after all.<br /> <br /> From that perspective Antarctica is probably an even bigger problem than the sea or jungles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a lodge in Antarctica.<br /> <br /> If a werewolf needs to go to Antarctica, they'll go there. They might be sent their on business, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T22:17:39-07:00","id":262665,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing with the sub-oceanic Shadow. It's mostly an ecosystem in balance. The same cannot be said about say, NYC. And it certainly doesn't holds true when you have some oil-leaks. Not that they reach that low to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T22:41:18-07:00","id":262670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=262665#post262665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing with the sub-oceanic Shadow. It's mostly an ecosystem in balance. The same cannot be said about say, NYC. And it certainly doesn't holds true when you have some oil-leaks. Not that they reach that low to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that it's more that the oceanic Shadow within sight of mortal shores is <i>contained</i>, that the mechanism of that containment is unclear, and that if there's an upset of balance therein it largely fails to become a problem that any but the most driven and obsessive and large/capable packs are inclined or able to deal with before it makes overtures toward the ports and coasts of Shadow.<br /> <br /> Basically, weird and terrifying shit manages to wander in from Far Outside* from time to time, but by and large the ripples for that need to make it to the Uratha's door in order for a problem to become evident and, as you note, the more prevalent vector for such disturbances is blowback from human endeavor.<br /> <br /> * (Or, taking the Banach-Tarski Space line Stew's mentioned, Deep Within)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T22:43:08-07:00","id":262672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=262665#post262665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing with the sub-oceanic Shadow. It's mostly an ecosystem in balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of no basis to assume this. Absence of humans doesn't mean spirits are behaving. This isn't WtA where environmental damage and social ills are the central root of werewolf concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T22:48:12-07:00","id":262676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=262672#post262672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of no basis to assume this. Absence of humans doesn't mean spirits are behaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, however, mean fewer are awakening without the involvement of established spirits who are hooked into an existing network of politics whose interactions mirror what we understand as &quot;the natural order.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T04:26:17-07:00","id":262765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=262676#post262676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does, however, mean fewer are awakening without the involvement of established spirits who are hooked into an existing network of politics whose interactions mirror what we understand as &quot;the natural order.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This, basically. Thanks for getting to me before I did, Satch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T04:32:43-07:00","id":262766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=262670#post262670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that it's more that the oceanic Shadow within sight of mortal shores is <i>contained</i>, that the mechanism of that containment is unclear, and that if there's an upset of balance therein it largely fails to become a problem that any but the most driven and obsessive and large/capable packs are inclined or able to deal with before it makes overtures toward the ports and coasts of Shadow.<br /> <br /> Basically, weird and terrifying shit manages to wander in from Far Outside* from time to time, but by and large the ripples for that need to make it to the Uratha's door in order for a problem to become evident and, as you note, the more prevalent vector for such disturbances is blowback from human endeavor.<br /> <br /> * (Or, taking the Banach-Tarski Space line Stew's mentioned, Deep Within)</div> </div> </div> </div>Such as this fucker: <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/j9pUHQN.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T05:48:09-07:00","id":262793,"title":"","content":"I have run a very sea-focused game as a break from a long-term Werewolf chronicle with my group. I had them build already-experienced werewolves for a plot set around a coastal Cornish village, featuring sunken container ships with strange cargo, eerie dwellers of the deep and spirits of the sea (and the Gull, I love the Gull). Also, a Sea Gift list.<br /> <br /> It was a lot of fun!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=262766#post262766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such as this fucker: <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/j9pUHQN.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> </div>The short-term Cornish pack I mentioned above? The final battle of that story arc was against TWO of these buggers on an island off the coast, and they were both buffed up with armour, weapons and further special abilities, <i>and</i> there was also a fishy mage-priest-thing that was multiple Mastery degree in various Arcana. I was heavily riffing off Slaine's Fomori - the Deeps were essentially praetorian guards for the priest.<br /> <br /> Two of the pack died but they took the Deeps and the priest down pretty handily.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I have a general love for things watery, coastal and marine, which will probably come through fairly strongly in the Bristol Hunting Ground in Werewolf 2e, and my Idigam Anthology short story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T06:37:04-07:00","id":262815,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking the Things That Shouldn't Have Been chapter in Predators would pretty much describe Earth-bound idigams in the new edition. Am I onto something here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T00:14:33-07:00","id":270647,"title":"","content":"The idigam are spirits, the things are flesh and blood, that's a pretty big difference to ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T03:09:44-07:00","id":270674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=270647#post270647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The idigam are spirits, the things are flesh and blood, that's a pretty big difference to ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about things that existed prior to the rise of the gauntlet, which would of had the power to make themselves a hide if they needed to. Also, review your posting tone, it comes off a lil more condescending than it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T04:24:27-07:00","id":270724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/261707-where-wolves-don-t-tread?p=262815#post262815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking the Things That Shouldn't Have Been chapter in Predators would pretty much describe Earth-bound idigams in the new edition. Am I onto something here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the original intent of the writers of those entries in Predators, but I would say that <i>some</i> of the entities therein could work as Earth-Bound - my personal preference is for both Earth-Bound <i>and</i> Things That Shouldn't Have Been to exist. I like my horrors from the past to be messy and not easily categorised <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T05:55:37-07:00","id":270747,"title":"","content":"Slaine meets Werewolf is something I can totally get behind.<br /> <br /> Also, some of the back-of-the-book Predators have possible origins explaining they were once spirits or are a type of Host/Shartha entity. Does that move them into being more spirit than flesh? Maybe, maybe not. They are largely unique creatures after all. And what would you say about the Breath, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:59:08-07:00","id":271013,"title":"","content":"I think as Uratha can be found in coastal towns and ports etc that they likely can and do interact with ocean-based spirits, like Storm Spirits or Drowning Spirits along with more conventional fish and sea-life based Spirits. There are likely some versions of fishing spirits and perhaps sea-vessels have their own spirits too. I don't think it would make up a huge chunk for Werewolf 2e if a book covering this got released, but a mini pdf with some suggestions and a New England coastal area for the City of Adventure would make a nice little thing that I'd buy for a few coins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}